{start_of_verse label="Verse"}
'Tis the [G]gift to be simple,
'Tis the [D]gift to be free,
'Tis the gift to come down where we [G]ought to be,
And [G]when we find ourselves
In the [C]place just [G]right,
'Twill be [D]in the valley of love and de[G]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When true [G]simplicity is [D]gained,
To [D]bow and to bend we shan't be a[G]shamed,
To [G]turn, turn will be our de[C]light,
Till by [G]turning, turning we [D]come round [G]right.
{end_of_chorus}
{x_end: G}
